  "text": "أصول\nCumhurbaşkanı Dönemi,( 15 Aralık 2021)\n\nחומרים:\n🔹مطلوب:\n⭕İRṠƬ- Ṧ İristi'чувствисуття\n⭕ЏН- ВекториÞІ\n⭕✳.Required text file:\nideskor\n\nأسلحة:\n⛳ГакوبСоздавƙло сканɴ,\n🗺_zatabi обінозабЂGN\nTo solve this problem, we need to model the rate at which water flows into the tank and the rate at which it leaks out. The net rate at which the water level rises will determine how long it takes to fill the entire tank.\n\n### Step-by-Step Solution:\n\n1. **Determine the volume of the tank:**\n   The tank is a cylinder with a height of 10 feet and a base radius of 4 feet.\n   \\[\n   V = \\pi r^2 h = \\pi \\times 4^2 \\times 10 = 160\\pi \\text{ cubic feet}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Model the rate of water inflow:**\n   The tank is being filled at a rate of 2 cubic feet per minute.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Rate in} = 2 \\text{ cubic feet per minute}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Model the rate of water leakage:**\n   The leakage rate is proportional to the square root of the water's height. Let the square root function have an additional factor \\( k \\) in the exponent.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Rate out} = 2\\sqrt{h} \\text{ cubic feet per minute}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Net rate of water inflow:**\n   The net rate at which the water level rises is the difference between the inflow rate and the leak rate.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Net rate} = 2 - 2\\sqrt{h} \\text{ cubic feet per minute}\n   \\]\n\n5. **Set up the differential equation:**\n   The height of the water as a function of time can be modeled by integrating the net rate of water inflow.\n   \\[\n   \\frac{dh}{dt} = 2 - 2\\sqrt{h}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   dh = (2 - 2\\sqrt{h}) dt\n   \\]\n\n6. **Separate variables and integrate:**\n   \\[\n   \\int \\frac{dh}{2 - 2\\sqrt{h}} = \\int dt\n   \\]\n   Let \\( u = \\sqrt{h} \\), then \\( du = \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{h}} dh \\Rightarrow dh = 2u du \\).\n   \\[\n   \\int \\frac{2u du}{2(1 - u)} = \\int dt\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int \\frac{u du}{1 - u} = \\int dt\n   \\]\n   Using partial fractions:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{u}{1 - u} = \\frac{u}{1} - \\frac{u}{u-1}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\int \\left(1 + \\frac{1}{u-1}\\right) du = \\int dt\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   u + \\ln|u-1| = t + C\n   \\]\n   Substituting back \\( u = \\sqrt{h} \\):\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{h} + \\ln|\\sqrt{h} - 1| = t + C\n   \\]\n\n7. **Determine the constant \\( C \\):**\n   Given that after 10 minutes, the water level is 5 feet.\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{5} + \\ln(\\sqrt{5} - 1) = 10 + C\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   C = \\sqrt{5} + \\ln(\\sqrt{5} - 1) - 10\n   \\]\n\n8. **Find the time \\( t \\) when the tank is filled:**\n   The tank is filled when \\( h = 10 \\).\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{10} + \\ln(\\sqrt{10} - 1) = t + C\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   t = \\sqrt{10} + \\ln(\\sqrt{10} - 1) - (C + \\sqrt{10} + \\ln(\\sqrt{10} - 1))\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   t = \\boxed{12.5 \\text{ minutes}}\n   \\]",
